  "targetText": "4. Use the actual norm budgetPythagoras and the adjoint contraction give the sum-of-squares budget. Apply the pair bound to the SAME actual fP,fV. An explicitly typed local have proves exactly this final conclusion before the outer witnesses are reconstructed.‖fP‖2+‖fV‖2≤‖f‖2⟹|C(fP,fV)|≤‖f‖22γ.Corresponding Lean step  have hFinal : ∀ f : Lp ℝ 2 J, (∫ z, f z ∂J)=0 →\n      ∃ fP : HP0,\n        HP0.subtypeL fP=condExpL2 ℝ ℝ (μ:=J) measurable_snd.comap_le f ∧\n        let fperp : Hperp := R f\n        let fV : HP0 := V0.adjoint fperp\n        B.adjoint (fperp : Lp ℝ 2 J)=HP0.subtypeL (ΓP0 fV) ∧\n        HP0.subtypeL (ΓP0 fV)=ΓP (HP0.subtypeL fV) ∧\n        ‖f‖^2=‖fP‖^2+‖fperp‖^2 ∧ ‖fV‖≤‖fperp‖ ∧\n        ‖fP‖^2+‖fV‖^2≤‖f‖^2 ∧ |C fP fV|≤‖f‖^2/(2*γ) := by\n    intro f hf\n    obtain ⟨fP,hGlobalFields⟩ :=",
